    # 14. HOUSEHOLD_ALLOCATION — Networth Invested + Cash Not Invested
    # ==================================================================
    # Matches repo files: "Percentage Networth Invested"
    #                     "Percentage cash not yet invested"
    #
    # These are two sides of the same coin — how households split their
    # assets between equities (invested) and cash/savings (not invested).
    # Grouped into one indicator for direct comparison.
    #
    # FRED — Federal Reserve Z.1 Financial Accounts + related:
    #   BOGZ1FL153064476Q  Households equity share of financial assets (Q, 1952->)
    #     This is THE definitive measure of US equity allocation.
    #     When it peaks → market top (dot-com 2000, 2021).
    #   MMMFFAQ027S  Money market fund assets (Q, 1974->)
    #   WRMFSL       Retail money funds (weekly, 1975->)
    #   SAVINGS      Savings deposits at commercial banks (monthly, 1959->)
    #   PSAVERT      Personal savings rate (monthly, 1959->)
    #     Rises in recessions (fear), falls in booms (confidence).
    #   BOGZ1FL154090005Q  Total household financial assets (Q, 1952->)
    #   BOGZ1FL153020005Q  Households total deposits (Q, 1952->)
    #   WDDNS          Demand deposits (weekly, 1975->)
    #
    # The cash vs equity balance is a powerful contrarian signal:
    #   High cash % → pessimism → bullish for future returns
    #   High equity % → euphoria → bearish for future returns
    {
